WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
The first film showed that a population needs survivors that reproduce.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.520
American chestnut roots still send up living sprouts.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.880
Why has that population not recovered?

4
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:16.733
Keep the same colors.

5
00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:22.833
Green marks living chestnut tissue, red marks blight, blue marks inherited

6
00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:25.093
resistance, and yellow marks seeds.

7
00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:28.093
A green root remains underground.

8
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:31.093
It sends a leafy sprout upward.

9
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.767
Red fungus grows into a crack in the bark.

10
00:00:35.947 --> 00:00:38.107
A canker widens around the young trunk.

11
00:00:39.327 --> 00:00:43.087
The trunk above it fades grey, while the protected root stays green.

12
00:00:44.547 --> 00:00:46.427
Soon that root sends up another sprout.

13
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.680
The cycle repeats.

14
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.340
The forest contains living chestnut stems, but the sprouts rarely become seed-making

15
00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:01.400
canopy trees. Living stems alone do not show that the population is recovering.

16
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.230
Freeze the cycle after a new sprout appears.

17
00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.970
No yellow seeds are present.

18
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:13.770
If every sprout dies before making seeds, can these sprouts rebuild a lasting

19
00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:14.770
population?

20
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.680
No. Each green sprout proves that living tissue remains, so the species is not

21
00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:33.100
extinct. But if sprouts die before making seeds, no new generation replaces the old

22
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.740
roots. In the wild, few sprouts make seeds.

23
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.200
Survival requires survivors to reproduce, not merely remain alive.

24
00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:45.243
How might people change that path?

25
00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:51.163
Breeders begin with American chestnuts and Chinese chestnuts that resist blight

26
00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:53.763
better. They cross the trees.

27
00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:57.103
Then they expose the offspring to blight.

28
00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:01.087
Blue resistance bars differ among the offspring.

29
00:02:02.487 --> 00:02:04.687
People choose the most resistant young trees.

30
00:02:05.927 --> 00:02:09.547
Then they cross those back to American chestnuts and test again.

31
00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.387
That is artificial selection.

32
00:02:13.647 --> 00:02:17.907
People choose which trees reproduce, instead of letting the environment alone

33
00:02:17.907 --> 00:02:18.907
decide.

34
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.760
The goal is not simply more differences.

35
00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.320
It is inherited resistance strong enough to help trees survive, make seeds, and grow

36
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.340
a next generation.

37
00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.860
Other traits still matter, but they cannot replace resistance to this fungus.

38
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:38.303
Crossing does not promise recovery.

39
00:02:39.703 --> 00:02:43.023
Breeders need repeated tests across many families and sites.

40
00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.823
These tests ask how well young trees survive and resist blight.

41
00:02:48.917 --> 00:02:52.417
Some scientists have also tried adding one gene from wheat.

42
00:02:53.697 --> 00:02:56.777
In tests, it helped American chestnuts resist blight.

43
00:02:58.057 --> 00:02:59.517
That work is still being checked.

44
00:03:00.857 --> 00:03:02.417
Both paths ask one question.

45
00:03:03.777 --> 00:03:07.017
Will enough trees survive, reproduce, and keep reproducing?

46
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.010
Return to the underground root.

47
00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.090
A sprout alone keeps the past alive.

48
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.490
Seed-making trees can begin the future.

49
00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:22.230
For this forest, recovery means living through blight and producing the next

50
00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.230
generation.

51
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.950
That is why the chestnut can remain alive yet fail to recover.

52
00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:34.750
The rule for this film is narrower: survival requires survivors to reproduce, not

53
00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:35.870
merely remain alive.
